{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the exact characterization \"a real exponent c is valid in Ben Green's Open Problem 19 if and only if c >= 4\", hence C = 4. Valid means: there is an absolute K > 0 such that for every density alpha in (0,1) and every sufficiently large n, every subset A of F_2^n x F_2^n of density at least alpha has a nonzero d for which the set of corners (x,y), (x+d,y), (x,y+d) in A has at least K alpha^c N^2 elements, N = 2^n. The upper bound (c = 4 is valid) formalizes Mandache's regularity argument on F_2^n with a finite weighted triforce inequality; the lower bound (no c < 4 is valid) formalizes the Behrend / Ruzsa-Szemeredi construction with random labellings and finite-product concentration. The proof uses only the standard axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
